==================== Input ====================
// A glued `-` after a call/paren in a value position is subtraction (dart-sass)
// and prints through the structured `SassExpr` printer with spaced operators.
// DIVERGES from Prettier (DIVERGENCES.md "value-glued-minus"):
// its value lexer keeps the glued `-` verbatim (`-` may start a number/ident,
// so no operator node forms), while the same glued `+` DOES get spaced.
// The same expression in a MEDIA-PRELUDE position is a different artifact:
// see media-query-operator-spacing.scss.
.a {
  width: map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm)-1;
  height: map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm)+1;
  // same rule inside SassScript function args (calculation args differ:
  // see calc-glued-minus.scss, where the glue is kept verbatim)
  margin: foo(map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm)-1, 0);
}
$y: map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm)-1;

==================== Output ====================
------------------
{ printWidth: 80 }
------------------
// A glued `-` after a call/paren in a value position is subtraction (dart-sass)
// and prints through the structured `SassExpr` printer with spaced operators.
// DIVERGES from Prettier (DIVERGENCES.md "value-glued-minus"):
// its value lexer keeps the glued `-` verbatim (`-` may start a number/ident,
// so no operator node forms), while the same glued `+` DOES get spaced.
// The same expression in a MEDIA-PRELUDE position is a different artifact:
// see media-query-operator-spacing.scss.
.a {
  width: map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm) - 1;
  height: map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm) + 1;
  // same rule inside SassScript function args (calculation args differ:
  // see calc-glued-minus.scss, where the glue is kept verbatim)
  margin: foo(map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm) - 1, 0);
}
$y: map-get($grid-breakpoints, sm) - 1;

